[33mcommit 9b5986c697ed3532aa749c60da4666ee7856d79c[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 20:56:28 2026 -0700

    C11-485: Keep the markdown web view in the visible host (#768)
    
    * C11-485: Keep the markdown web view in the visible host
    
    A markdown panel showed its toolbar but an empty body after area churn
    (closing a sibling area, splits) until the operator switched panels.
    MarkdownWebViewHost returned the renderer's one shared WKWebView from
    makeNSView, so a replacement host SwiftUI built and then discarded took
    the web view away from the host still on screen.
    
    Host it in MarkdownWebViewContainer: a host adopts the web view only
    while it is in a window, and a host that leaves its window hands it back
    to one still there. Same rule the browser panel uses for off-window
    replacement hosts.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-485: Hand the web view only to a host that is showing
    
    From review: a host counts as showing only in a visible window and
    without a hidden ancestor, so a closed window or hidden replacement
    cannot keep the web view. Skip redundant frame sets in layout, log
    claims and hand-backs in DEBUG, and test the same-window and
    closed-window cases.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

