[33mcommit 78528c8e71c21e583de202cbbebb8bc61e6da608[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 20:40:15 2026 -0700

    C11-486: Delegate marks show lineage baselines, not teal (#767)
    
    * C11-486: Delegate marks show lineage baselines, not teal
    
    Teal painted every delegate state, so a cold delegate read as a teal
    bar and blue stopped meaning cold. Color now means attention only: flag
    violet, then cache-cold blue, then the gray lifecycle ramp. A delegate
    draws one 1pt rule under its mark per delegate hop (display capped at
    two), per card E+ of design/delegate-marks/delegate-marks.html.
    
    - Depth walks delegated_by while each ancestor is itself a delegate
      (DelegateLineage, PanelAttentionIndex.delegationOwners); nothing new
      is persisted. A delegation change refreshes every delegate below it,
      across workspaces.
    - Sidebar WorkspacePulseMark and the Bonsplit tab mark (strip, sheet,
      rail) share BonsplitActivityMarkLineage geometry.
    - delegatedActivityHex and the teal branch of activityColorOverrideHex
      are gone; ActivityMarkTint holds the precedence.
    - Tooltip and panel-sheet text state the true depth past two, localized
      in all six locales.
    - Skill "Flags and delegates" describes the baseline and the gold rule.
    
    Bumps vendor/bonsplit to the c11-486 branch commit.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-486: Refresh delegate depth on restore, removal and in the sidebar
    
    Review fixes:
    - After a session restore, recompute every delegate's depth; restore
      replays panels before their workspaces are registered, so a delegate
      restored ahead of its delegate owner kept depth 1.
    - Panel removal and workspace prune refresh the delegates below the
      removed panels.
    - The descendant walk runs only when a panel's delegation changes.
    - The sidebar group projection carries lineage depth, so a depth-only
      change rebuilds the row's pulse marks.
    - Bonsplit: lineage marks sit on whole points in the 10pt slot.
    - Test and skill wording.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-486: Scope depth refresh on prune; refresh after debug restores
    
    Review round 2:
    - Prune refreshes only the delegates below panels it actually drops,
      so telemetry-driven prunes that drop nothing do no lineage work.
    - refreshAllDelegationDepths() runs after the debug session round-trip
      restores, as it does after a launch restore.
    - Bonsplit: lineage marks stay centred in the slot like other marks.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin @ Build <ops@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

