[33mcommit bb25b18b505612b600387794639dd211b381dfa1[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 19:18:17 2026 -0700

    Add c11 shortcuts list|set|reset: rebind keyboard shortcuts live from the CLI (#763)
    
    A defaults write to a shortcut.* key is invisible to a running c11 until
    relaunch. The new verbs and settings.shortcuts.* socket methods go through
    KeyboardShortcutSettings.setShortcut, the same path as the Settings
    recorder, so the menu, key handling and an open Settings window update at
    once. Bare `c11 shortcuts` still opens Settings.
    
    - Action script names are kebab-case case names (toggle-sidebar); legacy
      raw values (new-tab) resolve as hidden aliases.
    - Combos parse as ctrl+opt+shift+cmd+key or the display form; `none`
      unbinds. A script may not bind combos c11 or macOS keeps (Quit, Copy,
      Paste, the command palette, ...) or Shift plus a printable key; history
      actions keep the recorder's Cmd+[ / Cmd+] rule.
    - `set` and `reset` report other actions holding the same combo.
    - Settings' shortcut row no longer writes back a value that arrived by
      notification, which pinned a reset action to today's default.
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

