[33mcommit f4f35a67db25e8b8f8afb9df1cefd92740cfa313[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 23:28:58 2026 -0700

    Add a rebindable New Agent shortcut (⌥⌘A) (#750)
    
    * Add a rebindable New Agent shortcut (⌥⌘A)
    
    The A button's plain left-click had no keyboard path: New Panel opens a
    terminal and ⌘⇧A opens the picker, which still needs a row click.
    
    KeyboardShortcutSettings.Action.newAgent (defaults key shortcut.newAgent,
    label "New Agent", Navigation group beside New Panel) launches the
    default agent in the active workspace's focused area through the same
    launchDefaultAgentFromPanelBar path as the button, so a declined launch
    opens the picker with the reason. It is dispatched in AppDelegate's
    shortcut chain beside newSurface, listed under Area → New Panel, and the
    A button's tooltip keeps its resolved name · model · effort text and
    appends the chord.
    
    ⌥⌘A is the shipped default: ⌘ chords never reach the terminal, it pairs
    with ⌘⇧A (picker), and no c11 default, hardcoded menu item, AppDelegate
    chord or Ghostty default uses it. ⌃⌥A would take Meta-Ctrl-A from shells
    and editors and is VoiceOver's "read all".
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * New Agent: route by the key event's window; host routing test
    
    Review fixes for #750. The shortcut matcher now passes event.window to
    launchDefaultAgentForActiveWorkspace, which prefers it over the key and
    main windows, as ⌘T and the split shortcuts do. A DEBUG-only
    debugNewAgentLaunchHandler lets the host test capture the resolved
    workspace, pane and window without spawning a real agent.
    
    WindowRoutingShortcutTests.testNewAgentShortcutTargetsEventWindowFocusedPane
    presses ⌥⌘A at a window that is not key and checks the target is that
    window's focused pane, then rebinds to ⌃⌥A and checks the new chord
    dispatches. Drops a logic test that only compared two literals, and
    links the CHANGELOG entry to the PR.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

