[33mcommit eac6b1287cfce969458c798e57b150453cbb88b4[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 01:47:42 2026 -0700

    C11-334: Reject unknown flags before socket access (#737)
    
    * C11-334: Reject unknown flags before socket access
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: Validate inline focus workspace options
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: Preserve no-focus CLI options
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: Preserve no-focus pane move flags
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: preserve accepted CLI flags and text
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-6) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: Declare CLI flags explicitly and reject unsafe tails
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-6) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-334: Derive flag forms from rules and check declarations against parser reads
    
    Preflight now applies three rules to every declared spec instead of listing
    them per command: --json is the global output switch after any command,
    --name=value is rewritten to --name value for every declared value option,
    and alias spellings come from the parsers' alias tables. Text regions are
    declared for trailing command lines, browser text verbs and tmux words.
    
    A DEBUG-only read log in the shared option helpers records every flag a
    parser queries; testEveryFlagAParserReadsIsDeclared runs one argv per command
    path and fails on any name a parser reads that its declaration lacks.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-334: Read boundaries from command argv and normalize options in text verbs
    
    declaredCommandFlagPreflightSpec computed literal-tail boundaries from the
    process argv, so trailing-command parsers skipped validation. It now takes the
    command's own argv. Leading target options in = form are split before the verb
    is chosen, and browser type/fill/eval/add-script verbs check and rewrite their
    own options while unknown words stay text. respawn-pane and pipe-pane no longer
    put their target options into the command line.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-334: Keep option values out of the leading-target split and gate eval text on --script
    
    The leading --panel= split ran for every command and read the value of any
    other option as a target, so notify --body --panel=<ref> retargeted the
    notification and truncated its body. It now runs only for browser and markdown,
    whose declaration depends on the verb, and stops at the first option that is
    not a target. browser eval with --script takes no positional text, so an
    unknown flag there fails before browser.eval.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

