[33mcommit 554f2d765ce398a7b9be9db9234aad3b7be20ebf[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 09:04:58 2026 -0700

    C11-476: keep ringing an idle OpenCode seat after a native ring (#740)
    
    * C11-476: ring OpenCode again after a native ring whose working edge was lost
    
    OpenCode's plugin reports turn edges through the journal. A fast
    invitation turn's working boundary is dropped once the idle snapshot
    supersedes it (JournalMailboxBoundary.stillHolds), so the idle edge finds
    the turn already at its prompt and the ring epoch never moves. Every later
    envelope then logged once_per_idle until another turn. Pi and omp report
    edges through agent-hook directly, which always reaches the gate.
    
    A native acceptance now records the turn the invitation started, as a
    typed ring's Return does: an idle report since the ring's start opens the
    next idle period; otherwise the turn is working until one does. Seen
    edges are kept, so once-per-idle still holds.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-476: add the native repeat-mail guest probe
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

