[33mcommit 4f81f2d1f9076ca63d3ee2058d4add0d501a9288[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 07:53:21 2026 -0700

    C11-385: recover event log writes after an external delete, add a launch nonce, fix the EventLogTests parallel flake (#736)
    
    * C11-385: recover from an externally deleted event log on the next write, add a per-launch nonce, and fix the EventLogTests parallel flake
    
    - EventLog: each queue-confined write checks that the live path still names the open file; a delete or replace now reattaches immediately instead of at the next checkpoint (records in between went to the unlinked inode).
    - Instance ids carry a per-launch nonce (<label>-<pid>-n<8 hex>), so a reused pid never shares a log file (absorbs C11-384). Retention label extraction strips the nonce and then the pid; pre-nonce files keep their labels.
    - `c11 events tail --follow` polls inside an autoreleasepool per iteration.
    - EventLogTests.testSuccessfulTerminalRuntimeMakesEnrolledWorkspaceNonTransient: judge the records of its own workspace. Its await turns the main run loop, which releases Workspaces leaked by earlier tests; their deinit emits panel.closed + workspace.closed into the process-wide emitter's current log. A deterministic regression test injects that teardown.
    - skills/c11/references/events.md: instance id form and delete recovery.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-385: repair r1: instance id keeps an Int32 tail so shipped builds read the same retention label; tests_v2 finds the log by pid
    
    - Instance ids are <label>-<random positive Int32> (pid stays in log.opened). v1.2.0 and earlier strip exactly a trailing Int32, so the nonce form would have put nightly and production files under the 14-day development TTL in older builds.
    - tests_v2/test_send_key_ctrl.py selects the app's log by the pid in its log.opened record.
    - Checkpoint-recovery test asserts the marker before any append; docs and PR evidence aligned.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

