    C11-399: add a Sent view to the mailbox drawer (#732)
    
    * C11-399: add a Sent view to the mailbox drawer
    
    The dispatcher stamps the sending panel's UUID (reserved ext key) on accepted envelopes when from resolves to exactly one live panel, and records a small entry in the sender's _sent/ ledger. The drawer gains a Received | Sent switch that lists those entries with each recipient's read state, read from the recipients' own inbox and _read copies by id and verified against the stamp.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-399: document the Sent view and the sender stamp
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-399: attribute sent mail by the CLI's exact caller, show the cell for send-only panels, prove the scan bound
    
    The dispatcher no longer resolves from by name: the CLI attaches the calling panel and workspace as a reserved claim, honored only for a panel live in the dispatcher's own workspace and removed before delivery. A panel with a _sent ledger and nothing received now gets the cell. The scan test records actual listings and probes.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-399: give the cross-workspace collision test the addressed from that C11-478 stamps
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
