[33mcommit e6461a57534700bd9c7dae407f50c63b4baff715[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 05:31:17 2026 -0700

    C11-229: expose per-surface cwd, branch and worktree in tree --json (#731)
    
    * C11-229: expose per-surface cwd, branch and worktree in tree --json; skip git probe for remote workspaces
    
    tree --json terminal panels carry cwd/branch/worktree (null when unknown),
    projected from the same panelGitContexts/panelDirectories the sidebar chips
    read. Remote (c11 ssh) workspaces are no longer probed against the local
    filesystem and report null (absorbs C11-237).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-229: re-announce cwd in the location test so late shell reports cannot mask it
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-229: clear local git identity when a workspace turns remote
    
    A finished local probe left derived branch/worktree in get-metadata after
    workspace.remote.configure when the shell re-announced the same cwd. Clear
    the per-panel git context, branch, PR state and derived keys at the
    transition, and extend the socket test to cover it.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

