[33mcommit 7159459891dd82477d3aafaeae40684f87e12659[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 04:48:09 2026 -0700

    C11-387: markdown relative images follow the current document (#730)
    
    * C11-387: markdown relative images follow the current document after in-panel navigation
    
    The viewer's image scope was pinned to the first document's folder when the web
    view was created, so after navigating to a document in another folder the page
    asked for pic.png relative to the new folder and the handler served (or refused)
    it against the old one. The scheme handler now retargets its document root to the
    folder of the document being shown (same pinned-root rule, same folder-only scope)
    before each load, including back and forward. Adds a logic test and a guest
    acceptance script.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-387: acceptance script clicks the toolbar back/forward arrows
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-387: refetch document images after navigating to another folder
    
    WebKit reuses a resource for an identical URL for the page's lifetime, so after
    in-panel navigation the same relative name (pic.png) in another folder still
    showed the first document's image even once the native root followed. The viewer
    now appends ?e=<n> to image URLs after a load into a different folder; the native
    handler ignores the query and path validation is unchanged. First loads keep their
    URLs. Adds a policy test and clicks the toolbar arrows in the guest script.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

