[33mcommit 6f641c3475da1ec975dacb71c74c88173a42a5f8[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 04:42:22 2026 -0700

    C11-475: name each Claude native mail failure and report late confirmations (#728)
    
    * C11-475: name each Claude bridge failure and report late confirmations
    
    The bridge now sends a reason for every offer it cannot confirm:
    transcript_unavailable, inbox_unavailable, inbox_write_failed, or
    unconfirmed (the write succeeded but no record appeared within 1.8 s,
    which is where a crossSessionInbound refuse or hold lands). Reporting
    inside the app's two-second bound lets the log say why. After
    inbox_write_failed or unconfirmed it keeps watching the transcript for
    10 s between frame reads and sends accepted if the record appears, so a
    slightly late confirmation logs native_late_accept. A newer offer ends
    the watch.
    
    The backstop's Python job now runs tests/test_claude_mailbox_bridge.py
    against the exact-head CLI.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-475: log the consumer's named rejection reason as native_failure
    
    A rejected frame whose reason is one the Claude bridge names
    (transcript_unavailable, inbox_unavailable, inbox_write_failed,
    unconfirmed, unsupported_invitation) now resolves as native_<reason>, so
    the typed fallback row in _dispatch.log says why the native attempt
    failed. Any other or absent reason stays native_rejected, so Pi is
    unchanged and a consumer cannot write arbitrary text into the log.
    Frame handling moves into MailboxNativeDoorbell.consume so tests drive
    the same path as the stream loop.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-475: assert the refusal leg's exact native failure, and teach it
    
    The Claude guest check now requires the crossSessionInbound refusal to log
    doorbell_failed with reason native_unconfirmed on route claude_inbox, and
    the typed row that follows to carry native_route claude_inbox and the same
    native_failure. The c11 skill names the Claude bridge's failure reasons.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

