[33mcommit 65df54934955d8cfcf2ba1d1ee8e21355e6d49a7[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 04:18:07 2026 -0700

    C11-324: keep a hidden workspace's browser tab running (#719)
    
    * C11-324: keep a hidden workspace's browser tab running (browser keep-live)
    
    Per-panel keep-live parks the WKWebView slot unhidden beside the portal host
    while its workspace is hidden, so the page reports visible and timers, media
    and snapshots keep working. Socket browser.keep_live, CLI
    'c11 browser <panel> keep-live on|off|status', skill and socket docs, and a
    tests_v2 proof. Never touches workspace selection, focus or window order.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-324: host a keep-live browser whose workspace is not mounted
    
    Enabling keep-live on a browser with no portal entry (created after its workspace's
    background mount expired, or replaced while hidden) only set a flag. It now creates
    an anchor-less portal entry in the workspace's owning window, re-requests it when
    the web view is replaced, and releases it entirely on disable or close. A later
    bind from a mounted workspace adopts the entry. The guest test covers immediate
    and delayed creation, hidden replacement, a non-opted bystander tab, and direct
    workspace close (browser portal entry count via debug.portal.stats).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
