[33mcommit 7eee46f6717f5decea53e3497e9f7baa8c15f0aa[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 04:10:01 2026 -0700

    C11-473: deliver omp mailbox invitations through a native extension (#721)
    
    * C11-473: deliver omp mailbox invitations through a native extension
    
    Add omp_extension: omp-native-mail.ts reports working/idle edges and delivers the doorbell as a triggerTurn custom message at idle, accepted only by omp's own message_start. Wrapper exports the interactive marker and loads the extension by launch flag. Guest staging gains omp, pi-live and omp-live kinds, an omp proof, and a real-model smoke.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-473: cover stale omp sessions and settling turns in the consumer test
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-473: fix omp guest staging and make the live smoke robust to wrapped screens
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-473: publish omp idle only after real settle
    
    omp's recovery paths start a continuation before emitting the old agent_end. Report idle only once isIdle() is true and no newer turn, session or shutdown superseded the end notification; the bounded poll could publish idle during an automatic retry and strand the native invitation.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * C11-473: retry a busy omp rejection natively and supersede stale deliveries
    
    A busy native_rejected on omp happens before any side effect and omp has no typed composer reader, so a sticky typed fallback stranded the mail for the whole session. It now retries at the next ring (cap applies); hard failures and other routes still stick. A delivery waiting for idle is superseded by a session switch. The live smoke now fails when the model does not claim the mail.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

