    C11-472: deliver Claude mail through its session inbox (#714)
    
    * C11-472: bridge Claude mailbox invitations through its session inbox
    
    Add a launch-scoped async hook with bound-session confirmation and typed
    fallback when the inbox feature or listener is unavailable. Keep tokens in
    memory and retire the bridge with its harness or subscription.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-472: add guest acceptance and native route controls
    
    Exercise real Claude sessions through the packaged wrapper, preserve the
    Stop drain, and provide a native-only diagnostic opt-out. Bound the bridge's
    autorelease lifetime and keep transport-test cleanup deterministic.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-472: retain the failed acceptance window before cleanup
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-472: prove unsupported launches never subscribe
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-472: harden bridge frames deadlines and late transcript freshness
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
