[33mcommit e6f4f9394d75a7bb5f995da64a641f5d6de11a64[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 22:28:47 2026 -0700

    C11-471: deliver Pi mailbox invitations without touching the composer (#713)
    
    * C11-471: deliver Pi mailbox invitations through its native extension
    
    Add an acknowledged native socket route with typed fallback, preserve draft and inbox state, and keep Pi placeholder lifecycle edges live. Include controlled-provider guest staging and repeatable acceptance proof.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-471: clarify native and typed mailbox quick starts
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-471: localize native mailbox protocol errors
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-471: preserve acknowledgements across the Pi idle edge
    
    The live guest showed idle telemetry opening the next delivery before a later settled handler cleared its acceptance callback. Clear the old slot before publishing idle.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-471: reopen the Pi mailbox gate for a fresh idle session
    
    The real guest /new proof showed a session-start event without an agent-settled event. Report observed idle before returning from session_start so the command Return cannot hold mail.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    * C11-471: verify native subscriber ancestry from the socket peer
    
    Accept detached hook descendants of the live foreground harness while rejecting unrelated callers and reused process identities.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Codex (gpt-6-astra) <noreply@openai.com>

