[33mcommit 5cba7ea9e23972870759ae5aa08fbc81754d13b5[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 18:12:08 2026 -0700

    Mailbox doorbell: press Return on a stranded doorbell line (#710)
    
    About 2% of doorbell rings typed the line and then refused the Return at the
    pre-Return check, usually because the agent's journal showed a turn open (a
    new turn started during the paste, or the journal lagged the prompt gate).
    The line was left in the composer, and later looks only logged
    `doorbell_recheck stranded` until the operator cleared it.
    
    A look that reads the whole line back exactly at an idle prompt now presses
    Return on it, with the same pre-Return checks and every other ring check
    except once-per-idle (which guards retyping). In the idle period whose ring
    was refused, a defer, a cap, a busy read, or a visible prefix looks again
    instead of stopping at once-per-idle. A pressed Return counts toward the
    cap; one refused before the key does not. Refusals log `turn_open` or
    `interruption_settling` when the journal caused them.
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

