[33mcommit de42f7f567278976ca5b6c59dac58225fa7ac977[m
Author: Atin <ops@demo.lan>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 18:09:34 2026 -0700

    Drop panels onto sidebar workspaces through an AppKit drop view (#711)
    
    * Drop panels onto sidebar workspaces through an AppKit drop view
    
    The per-row SwiftUI .onDrop never received Bonsplit's AppKit panel drag, so
    dragging a panel onto a workspace card did nothing. An NSView over the
    sidebar rows now registers for the panel drag type, takes hit tests only
    while a panel drag is in flight, outlines the card under the cursor in gold,
    and on release moves the panel into that workspace's focused area without
    switching the operator away. The window observer view no longer answers hit
    tests, since it sat above the sidebar in the drag path.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * Panel drop: follow a workspace's last panel, steadier targeting
    
    Review fixes. Dropping the only panel of the selected workspace closes that
    workspace, so the operator now follows the panel instead of landing on a
    neighbour. The drag gate checks the event type before anything else, since
    hit tests run it on every keystroke, and it admits modifier and periodic
    events mid-drag. The transfer and source workspace are read once per drag
    session, the target holds across the gap between cards, and the highlight
    clears if the sidebar leaves the window. The window observer view steps out
    of hit testing only during a panel drag, so Settings still moves by its
    background. The c11 skill says where a dropped panel lands.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Atin <operator.at.work@example.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

